Spec: Deadline entity

Purpose:
  The Deadline entity: one dated obligation of a CourseRealization, such as `Assignment 1` due on `2026-09-21`.
  It carries a date and a title and nothing else, so a realization can hold many of them: one per assignment,
  exam or report the group owes. A view-less, route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  whose `Deadline` column owns the affordances that create, edit and remove one, and by
  ../semester/semester.sdd, which draws each one as a circle.

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd

Must:
  A Deadline has a reference to exactly one CourseRealization stored as a plain id, a date and a non-empty
    free-text title; it carries nothing else, per ./deadlines.sdd's Purpose.
  The CourseRealization reference is declared as a foreign key, so the database enforces it and cascades a removed
    CourseRealization to its Deadlines; no service hand-deletes Deadlines.
  Several Deadlines may share one date, since a realization can owe more than one thing the same day, so the table
    carries no uniqueness rule and a duplicate date is never rejected.
  A Deadline's date is not checked against its CourseRealization's Semester period or its NoTeachWeeks, because a
    deadline is an obligation rather than teaching: it may fall in a break week or, stored over the MCP write tools,
    outside the Semester the weekly view covers.
  @DeadlineService.add_deadline validates that the CourseRealization id exists (through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd) and that the title is non-empty, rejecting
    with @UnknownRealizationError or @InvalidDeadlineError before storage.
  @DeadlineService.update_deadline applies the same checks and keeps the CourseRealization the Deadline already
    belongs to; it rejects an unknown id with @UnknownDeadlineError.
  @DeadlineService.delete_deadline removes one Deadline and leaves the realization's other Deadlines untouched,
    rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownDeadlineError.
  @DeadlineService.list_deadlines_for_realization returns one CourseRealization's Deadlines ordered by date, which is
    what ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view-model reads once for every week row's `Deadline` cell and
    every per-Deadline dialog it renders.
  @DeadlineService.list_deadlines_for_range returns every Deadline dated between two dates across all
    CourseRealizations, ordered by date, which is what ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner reads for its
    circles.
  @DeadlineRepository in ./ports.py exposes get, list Deadlines for a CourseRealization or a date range, and add,
    update and delete operations backing ./services.py.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Must not:
  This package must not gain a view.py or routes.py: a Deadline is created, edited and removed only through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's `Deadline` column, so the feature's affordances and routes stay owned there.

Scenario: A realization's deadlines are removed with it
  Given a CourseRealization has two Deadlines
  When the CourseRealization is removed
  Then neither Deadline remains

Scenario: Admin removes one Deadline from the weekly view
  Given a CourseRealization's weekly table shows two Deadlines in its `Deadline` column
  And the admin is logged in
  When the admin confirms the first Deadline's delete dialog, which names the Deadline and its date
  Then the `Deadline` column shows the other one and the realization keeps its Lessons and its other entries

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @Deadline in ./domain.py, and ./ports.py, ./services.py and ./repository_sqlite.py with
    @DeadlineService validating through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd